board:0007 -- per-object ACTION-METHOD base-loss cascade (native SEGV in CYPRUS1/INDIA1/SAUDI1 self-play).

The engine dispatches per-object periodic "action" methods indirectly with DI = the object's DGROUP NEAR
offset.  Ghidra typed the method's DI-relative derefs as HOST-pointer derefs of `param_2` -> a base-loss:
on native the near offset (e.g. 0x9afc) is dereferenced as an absolute host address and SEGVs (fault-addr
0x9b15 = param_2+0x19).  AZER1 never reaches these methods; CYPRUS1/INDIA1/SAUDI1 do, so their native
self-play crashes while wasm's does not -- exactly the base-dependent divergence class this port hunts.

Fixed for the two methods CYPRUS1's early self-play reaches (crash advanced 9afc -> bc0c -> clear):
  FUN_0000_9afc (asm 0x9afc `incw 0x19(%di)` ... lcall f69:a61a=9caa)
  FUN_0000_bc0c (asm 0xbc0c `orb 0x40,0x16(%di)` `orb 0x44,0x17(%di)` `incw 0x1f(%di)` ... 9caa)
Both are uniformly DS-relative on DI -> rebase the derefs onto g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)param_2.  9caa still
receives the raw NEAR offset (the asm keeps DI across the lcall).  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.
AZER1 self-play stays byte-identical (228 frames); CYPRUS1 native no longer crashes (runs 52+ frames).
(A residual CYPRUS1 unit-spawn-cadence divergence + siblings 26545/27534/29715/30979 are board:0007 continued.)

